## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **4-partition kebab layout (Design·Critic·Image·Video by type)** — Director rejected on live review: «такой порядок не очень». The type-grouping merged both tracks' plans/critics, read worse than per-track. Reworked into two fields (Image/Video), each with its own designer+critic. (Committed only the two-field version.)
- **Polina's proposed canon-staleness fix (skill-rule + slug-reference scan)** — REJECTED (told Director). Two reasons: (1) wrong layer — a skill is authoring-time advisory, can't enforce reverse-invalidation of already-APPROVED plans (that's runtime/reconciler). (2) her slug-reference scan MISSES her own SH16 example — SH16 has objects:[], never references gym_equipment; the problem is «canon APPEARED in the location», not «referenced canon changed».
- **replay-pilot NOT run** — deliberately deferred (agent-layer changes) to avoid disrupting live E16 Inngest/DB. Must run when episode idle. Changes are byte-identical at defaults so expected to pass.

